+Rationale: this scenario intentionally lets FRAME_TIMEOUT fire and then checks
+the timeout cleanup. Before this change mode was still 0, so the scoreboard
+enforced the 14 normal register writes on the first cleanup write and reported
+"SYNC_FAIL ordered role writes cycle=828 tx=14" instead of reaching the intended
+error_code==5 check. Setting mode=1 only for this timeout scenario keeps the
+14-write ordered check active for every normal boot (including the final reset
+recovery boot) and lets the deliberate cleanup transactions be checked by the
+whitelist/one-outstanding rules. No DUT RTL, timeout constant or acceptance
+threshold changed.
